  "overview": {
    "text": "Spirited Away (Japanese title: Sen to Chihiro no Kamikakushi) is a 2001 Japanese animated fantasy film written and directed by Hayao Miyazaki for Studio Ghibli. Ten-year-old Chihiro enters a spirit world with her parents; after they are transformed into pigs, she takes a job in a bathhouse for spirits and tries to save them. The bathhouse, filled with unusual beings including a dragon and a witch, gives the film its distinctive setting. Chihiro’s efforts to adapt and act courageously make it a coming-of-age story. The film won the Academy Award for Animated Feature at the 2003 ceremony, a major international recognition for the work.",
